SCOPE

This file describes the current Visual Enhancer 17.0.0.0 C++ application,
its third-party source and headers, and the runtimes used in its Windows
release packages. The application no longer uses the previous embedded
Python/PySide package, mpv, yt-dlp, or Python package wrappers.

Source paths below are relative to Build/ in this repository unless a
native (dev)/ path is given. Runtime paths are relative to the end-user
release directory (Visual Enhancer/): executables and Qt libraries are at
its root, media tools and native engines are in bin/, and application
resources are in resources/. Settings and caches use Windows per-user
storage; outputs/ and logs/ are relative to the release directory.
Native SDKs and engine development files are maintained separately and
are not included in the application source upload.

This file names each component, its known licensing, where it is shipped,
and where to read its version and available license text. Re-audit this
notice when a component or runtime version changes; bundled dependencies
and their terms can change between builds.

"Version:" lines identify the checked source/build version or the
authoritative version record: source headers, DLL version resources,
runtime-manifest.json, Qt SPDX inventories, or a tool's -version output.
Headers, command-line tools, Qt media libraries, and other media DLLs may
come from different upstream releases.

Source trees, license texts, attribution inventories, and upstream URLs
are not by themselves a declaration that every corresponding-source or
relinking obligation has been fulfilled. Any distributed copyleft binary
must be accompanied by the source/build materials and other provisions
required by its applicable license.

Nothing in this file grants rights beyond the applicable third-party license.
